hether it accumulates across the full suite, or ownership under repeated by-path loads"],"finding":"The plan introduces/repairs a shared module cache (the 'cache-first guard') but does not specify the RETIRE/cleanup or ownership dimension of that cache. The reported defect is itself a cross-test state LEAK ('leaks marklas state under serial full-suite ordering'), so a fix that merely makes the loader prefer a cached module identity could still leave the underlying cache accumulating or serving stale entries across a full suite. The plan proves same-source identity and a different-source control, but does not state who populates the cache, when entries are evicted, or that the guard is safe against the leak recurring for a different module.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"feee37659c4281a71","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Phase 2 plan / AC 'Deleting the cache-first guard returns the held-out test to RED'","norm_id":"n431068fa5bb96548","priority":0.0,"reason":"veto:absence-refuted","recalled":false,"scenarios":[],"severity":"none","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.25,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"no","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"no","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"no","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"none","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Reconcile the proposed cache-first guard + identity oracle against bug 9f0b's shipped `_load_module` (tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/diffing/test_differ.py) and its pinning test `test_load_module_identity.py` (and the conftest cache-first seeding): state in the RCA whether the fix reuses/extends the existing guard or why the rich-text-cutover leak requires a distinct mechanism.","cohort":["A1"],"criteria":["A1"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.95,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/diffing/test_differ.py:47-55 already implements a cache-first lookup guarded by `cached.__file__ == str(path)` — 'Mirrors the cache-first lookup differ._load_mutation() already does.'","tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/diffing/test_load_module_identity.py pins BOTH invariants against the REAL helper: 'SAME name + SAME path must return the SAME object' and 'SAME name + DIFFERENT path must NOT return the cached module', matching the plan's proposed `test_by_path_loader_preserves_module_identity_for_the_same_source` plus 'different-source control'.","tests/unit/conftest.py:50-52 and tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/conftest.py:71-74 already implement 'already-seeded flat sys.modules keys win' cache-first semantics for the shadow/engine split — the same defect class the plan describes.","The plan text never cites 9f0b, `_load_module`, or `test_load_module_identity.py`; AC 'Prior related tickets are inspected and cited' is where this reconciliation would land but the plan gives no indication 9f0b is on that list."],"finding":"Phase 2's proposed 'cache-first guard' and held-out same-source/different-source module-identity oracle duplicate an already-shipped, already-tested mechanism (bug 9f0b): the diffing suites' `__file__`-guarded cache-first `_load_module` and its pinning test `test_load_module_identity.py`. The plan does not reference this prior art or state whether it will 